  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_017 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250. All completed experiments are multiprofile, leaving the singleprofile multimodal dimension entirely unexplored. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (weighted) choices are well-supported by the data. Question: config_023 tests whether singleprofile multimodal (no aggregation step) with the best-known components can match or exceed the multiprofile ceiling. This is critical because singleprofile removes the aggregation bottleneck and could either (a) match multiprofile at lower cost, or (b) reveal that multiprofile aggregation is essential. Why this is the best use of experiment 7: With only 3 experiments remaining, exploring this untested architectural axis is the highest-information experiment. If singleprofile performs comparably, it opens a cheaper path; if it underperforms significantly, it confirms multiprofile + transformer is the right direction and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), since it eliminates the transformer aggregation step present in the multiprofile configs (3.6–4.85 hrs) while retaining the imagenet_vit_l image encoding."
}

